# Where the frontend connects (packages/connect). Nothing here is needed for
# local development: `pnpm dev:local mero-forms` starts merod local, deploys the
# contract and writes .env.development.local with the three values below.
#
# VITE_CALIMERO_TARGET=local
# VITE_CALIMERO_NODES=http://127.0.0.1:2501,http://127.0.0.1:2502,http://127.0.0.1:2503
# VITE_CALIMERO_BUNDLE=<the bundle hash dev:local uploaded>

# A production build (`vite build`) connects to a Calimero Cloud cluster by name
# and refuses to start without these two. Set them where the bundle's frontend
# is built (the release workflow), never per developer.
VITE_CALIMERO_CLUSTER=
VITE_CALIMERO_MIN_RELEASE=

# Optional: try this zone's nodes first; another node directory (staging);
# another package or a pinned version to create instances from.
# VITE_CALIMERO_ZONE=
# VITE_CALIMERO_DIRECTORY=
# VITE_CALIMERO_PACKAGE=com.calimero.mero-forms
# VITE_CALIMERO_VERSION=

# Public links (Connect → Public links). Optional.
#
# Where links open. A page the cluster serves from the bundle reaches only the
# cluster (its CSP), so it cannot load Cloudflare's Turnstile widget: to put a
# captcha on links, serve the `/f` page from an origin of your own (e.g. the
# Vercel deploy, https://mero-forms.vercel.app) and have the node's operator
# add that origin to the node's allowed origins. Unset: this page's origin.
# VITE_PUBLIC_FORM_ORIGIN=
#
# The Turnstile site key the public page shows for forms whose captcha the
# workspace checks itself (`turnstile`): the public half of the widget whose
# secret the node's operator holds as TURNSTILE_SECRET. An admin may set the
# team's own instead (Team → Captcha).
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
